# Bytecode caches land beside the sources, generated ones included. The generator owns
# `src/hook0/generated/` outright and sweeps away whatever it did not write, so a cache left there
# is reported as removed on the next regeneration — harmless, since Python rebuilds it, but noise
# in a report whose whole point is to be empty. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` keeps it from appearing
# at all.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool, test and property-search state
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Build artefacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
